{title: 503 - A Quiet Place}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #503 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 503}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]There is a [E7]quiet place,
[Am]Far from the [C7]rapid pace where [F]God can [A7]soothe my [Dm]troubled [Em]mind.
[Gm]Sheltered by [C7]tree and flow'r,
[F]There in my [Dm]quiet hour with [Am]Him my [F#m]cares [B7]are [E]left be[Dm7]hind[G].
[C]Whether a [E7]garden small,
[Am]Or on a [C7]mountain tall, New [F]strength and [E7]courage [Am]there I [C7]find;
[Am]Then from this [Dm7]quiet place
[Em7]I go pre[A7]pared to face a [Dm]new day With [G7]love for all man[C]kind.
{end_of_verse}
